  "summary": "Brunswick County (NC) commissioners voted unanimously for a 30-day pause on new ALPR purchases and to form a review committee after discovering the sheriff's office has 15 operational Flock cameras despite contracting for only 8, plus a recent SBI investigation into a deputy's alleged Flock misuse. The article also details a $4M Axon contract and references New Hanover County's recent Flock cancellation.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Brunswick County commissioners agreed Monday to a 30-day pause on purchasing any new automated license plate readers and to create a committee to discuss the technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flax says due to an oversight by Flock, seven of the eight original cameras on private land were never removed, meaning the county has 15 operational cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    },
    {
      "quote": "Even with audit logs, Flock cannot prevent curiosity lookups, personal tracking, improper misuse, targeting individuals without probable cause",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "a Wrightsville Beach police officer was indicted for misusing the county and town's Flock cameras as well.",
      "paragraph_idx": 25
    }
  ],
